  "review": {
    "base": "master",
    "branch": "m3/eclipse-entry-free-traversal-20261102",
    "title": "Traverse indexed sorted-map key/value lanes without Entry projections"
  },
  "review_statement": "## Problem and change\n\nInternal sorted-map traversal was allocating Entry projections and weak references even when callers only consumed keys or values. Reuse the existing slot cursor for direct key/value traversal, clear bounded views through a key cursor, and partition values directly. Public Entry APIs remain available.\n\nPreserve sorted order, bounds, epochs, comparator/procedure failures, view lifecycle, and null-procedure diagnostics. Add source-pinned differential and public-adapter tests.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Actual fork and isolated receiving reactors: **254 tests each, zero failures/errors/skips**, on the preserved pre-format source.\n- Formatting-only final changes were recompiled and all **9 new tests** passed.\n- TreeSortedMap public/protected descriptors are identical.\n- Checkstyle executed: all **281 production findings match baseline**, zero added production/body findings. Two new-test license headers conflict with the inherited fixed-header rule and remain an open gate.\n\nThe original destructive-comparator baseline hang is retained in canonical evidence as a counterexample; no equivalence claim is made for that hanging case. Concurrent entry-chain families are outside this packet.\n\n## Canonical execution\n\nCanonical recipe: `com.synexia.m3jdk.CollectionsContractRefinement20261017`, source revision **7af83c5ee4ad166d8cd45c6c33822debabd705ca**, review https://github.com/hsoliwal/com.synexia/pull/15427. Product bytes were emitted by actual qualified SDK Results and the second receive changed zero files. The canonical recipe and executable receiver remain in Synexia.\n",
